                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "73386ea2-049f-3ead-a4d9-8e071bbad124",
                        "entry_id": "1f8f0cb6-8fc6-353a-b69e-182df691ac90",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Statut d’État."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "03971572-3e14-438c-830d-78232d5a3264",
                                "sense_id": "73386ea2-049f-3ead-a4d9-8e071bbad124",
                                "text": "Support for what has been called self-determination would be less automatic or likely than was the case in the era of decolonization. Existing governments would agree to be open to considering bids for statehood in cases where there is historical justification, a compelling rationale, demonstrated support by the population in question and viability of the territory, including its potential ability to meet its obligations as a sovereign entity.",
                                "translation": "Le soutien à ce que l'on appelle l'autodétermination serait moins automatique ou probable qu'à l'époque de la décolonisation. Les gouvernements en place accepteraient d'examiner les demandes d'accession au statut d'État dans les cas où il existe une justification historique et convaincante, un soutien démontré par la population concernée et la viabilité du territoire, y compris dans sa capacité potentielle à remplir ses obligations en tant qu'entité souveraine."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d35d9dad-3d5f-47de-8d58-ee8b9eb07f5b",
                                "sense_id": "73386ea2-049f-3ead-a4d9-8e071bbad124",
                                "text": "Lecompton - in U.S. history, a reference to the town in Kansas Territory where a constitution for statehood was drawn up in 1857 by pro-slavery men."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
